      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RED ROCQUETTE (10) handy two-year-old ready to get off the mark at her third race start. Sat up on the speed in the soft conditions and found plenty with a narrow second over 1200m at Goulburn. This is much easier and no excuses here. MINERS MATE (8) resumed from a spell with a career best second over 1000m at Quirindi. Has further improvement to come and not sure where he races from the gate. Each-way. MR CACCIATORE (1) his two career starts have been encouraging and he comes back another level for this. Chipped away late with the 59kg when fourth over 1000m at Scone two-and-a-half weeks ago. Sure to run well. DAISY DUCK (5) is deep into the prep and the tongue-tie comes off. Worked hard from the wide gate and was a spent force in the straight with a fading tenth over 1000m at Tamworth. Better map today and can return to form.",
